    "recommendations": "Posting visible address numbers at the primary access point and ensuring they remain legible from the street could improve responder navigation, particularly given the length of the driveway. Because the property has a single access point serving both the main and secondary buildings, coordinating with local fire and emergency services to pre-identify a designated staging area near the entrance could support more effective operations. Trimming or managing dense vegetation along the driveway corridor where it may reduce driver sightlines or limit apparatus maneuvering would support responder movement. Noting the limited rear access to structures when communicating with emergency services may assist personnel in pre-planning appropriate response positioning."
